flow "Raft membership change (joint consensus)"
summary "Transitions cluster membership through a joint configuration requiring dual quorums so split brains cannot form, even when removing the current leader."
tags consensus raft reconfiguration
level advanced
source "https://raft.github.io/raft.pdf"
related distributed-systems/raft-consensus

group old "C_old (S1, S2, S3)"
node s1 "S1 (Leader)" service in=old tone=primary
node s2 "S2" service in=old
node s3 "S3" service in=old
group added "Joining node"
node s4 "S4" service in=added hidden
edge s1 > s2
edge s1 > s3
edge s1 > s4 hidden
edge s2 > s3 noarrow
edge s2 > s4 hidden noarrow
edge s3 > s4 hidden noarrow
array cfg "Active config & quorum" keys=config,quorum = C_old "2/3 of {S1,S2,S3}"

scenario joint-consensus "Two-phase joint consensus avoids split quorums"
  step c-old "Cluster starts in C_old = {S1, S2, S3}"
    "Jumping directly from `C_old` to `C_new` is unsafe: different servers switch at different times, allowing two disjoint quorums to elect two leaders in the same term."
    state s1 success
    callout s1 "Direct switch risks 2 leaders"
  step enter-joint "Phase 1: append and replicate C_old,new"
    "To replace S1 with S4 (`C_new = {S2, S3, S4}`), leader S1 appends joint config `C_old,new`. Immediately on append, every commit and election requires a majority of **both** `C_old` AND `C_new`."
    detail "Each server always adopts the latest configuration entry in its log immediately upon appending it, even before commit. Before starting reconfiguration, Raft lets brand-new servers join as non-voting members to catch up their logs without creating availability gaps."
    show s4,s1-s4,s2-s4,s3-s4
    state s4 active
    send s1 > s2 "Append C_old,new"
    send s1 > s3 "Append C_old,new" with
    send s1 > s4 "Append C_old,new" with
    label cfg#config "C_old,new"
    label cfg#quorum "maj(Old) AND maj(New)" with
    state cfg active with
  step commit-joint "C_old,new commits with dual majorities"
    "S2, S3, and S4 acknowledge. Both `C_old` (`{S1,S2,S3}`) and `C_new` (`{S2,S3,S4}`) reached a majority, so no conflicting leader can be elected."
    send s2 > s1 "ack"
    send s3 > s1 "ack" with
    send s4 > s1 "ack" with
    state s2,s3,s4 success

scenario remove-leader "Removing the current leader cleanly" from=joint-consensus/commit-joint
  step append-new "Phase 2: S1 appends C_new = {S2, S3, S4}"
    "Now that `C_old,new` is committed, S1 appends `C_new = {S2, S3, S4}` — a configuration that does **not** include S1 itself. S1 keeps managing replication without counting its own vote in `C_new`."
    send s1 > s2 "Append C_new"
    send s1 > s3 "Append C_new" with
    send s1 > s4 "Append C_new" with
    label cfg#config "C_new"
    label cfg#quorum "2/3 of {S2,S3,S4}" with
    callout s1 "S1 manages log until C_new commits"
  step step-down "C_new commits: S1 steps down"
    "S2, S3, and S4 acknowledge `C_new`. The instant `C_new` is committed, S1 steps down and leaves the cluster."
    detail "Once removed, S1 stops receiving heartbeats and may time out and send `RequestVote` with higher terms. To prevent removed nodes from disrupting the live cluster, Raft servers ignore `RequestVote` RPCs received within the minimum election timeout of hearing from a current leader."
    send s2 > s1 "ack"
    send s3 > s1 "ack" with
    send s4 > s1 "ack" with
    state s1 disabled
    label s1 "S1 (Removed)"
    callout s1 "Steps down once C_new commits"
  step new-leader "Remaining cluster elects S2 safely"
    "`{S2, S3, S4}` hold every committed entry and elect S2 as the new leader under `C_new` with zero downtime and zero split-brain window."
    send s2 > s3 "RequestVote"
    send s2 > s4 "RequestVote" with
    label s2 "S2 (New Leader)"
    state s2,s3,s4,cfg success
